⭐ **Row 3 jumped the queue and shipped first (16 Aug), as a GENERAL tutorial.**
A real sponsor (Pixocial / BeautyPlus) approached the channel on 12 Aug asking
for a media kit and rates. The kit in `media-kit/` was built from live analytics
to answer that email — but the user's call was to keep the *video* generic: no
brand named, no real figures, placeholders throughout. The case study informed
the script; it never appears in it. Search data ranked this 3rd, so shipping it
first was an editorial call, not a data one.

**Row 1 shipped next (16 Aug).** Its trap is the one nobody teaches: Canva's
**1 MB stroke limit per design**, which stops *saving* your drawings without
stopping you drawing them. Straight from Canva's own help pages. Note the slate
row said "pressure" — Canva's docs mention pressure sensitivity nowhere, so
that was dropped rather than asserted. Shape assist (draw, then hold still for
one second) carried the second Short.

**Row 2 shipped 18 Aug.** Its trap is the sharpest the channel has found: crop
an image in Canva, export to PDF, and the uncropped original is still inside the
file — Canva's own docs say so, and a PDF editor gets it back. The fix is the
**Flatten PDF** checkbox. The second trap is **Include notes**, sitting right
next to it, which emails an investor your private speaker notes.

**Row 4 shipped 18 Aug.** Trap = Advanced options, the link sitting *under* the
Continue button: Output → Individual designs, and Name each page using → your
name column. Miss it and Bulk Create hands you one fifty-page file and an hour
of renaming.

**Next up: row 5, the 2027 calendar — and it is time-critical.** 336/28d, and
next-year calendars get built Aug–Oct, so this is the one row on the slate with
a deadline. The certificates outro already teases it.

Rows 1 and 8 are deliberately view-first rather than funnel-first: with the ads
off and 76% of traffic coming from search, the channel needs the search equity
as much as the conversions. Everything else ends at a £4.99 pack.

Cadence: **2 long-form/week + 1–2 loop-grammar Shorts cut from each**,
alternating a GAP row with a PROVEN-QUERY sequel. Sequels link the old video in
the description and pin a comment on the old video pointing to the new one.

