  Trap = Canva's own help page describes PDF Print as offering a "color profile (RGB or CMYK) selection option" AND lists CMYK colour profile options among the features restricted to Pro/Teams/Education/Nonprofit. So PDF Print works on free; the CMYK choice inside it does not, and your print file leaves in RGB for someone else's software to convert. Neons collapse, deep colours survive. Second trap = bleed, which IS free: tick crop marks and bleed and run the background past the canvas, or a millimetre of guillotine drift leaves a white stripe.
  Strongest funnel since the pitch deck — anyone making a lookbook has products to sell and a print budget. The print-shop brief PDF may be worth the £4.99 on its own.
