## Slate 3 — ranked 1 Sep 2026 on the CLEAN window

Ranked on `--days 28` (4 Aug → 1 Sep), which is the first window with **zero
ADVERTISING views** — 78% of views are YouTube search. A 90-day window was tried
first and thrown away: it reaches back into the pre-4-Aug ad spend, which put
30% of views on ADVERTISING and made ad-boosted videos look like organic demand.
**Never rank on a window that includes ad spend.**

Every row below was grepped against the 435-video catalogue AND the do-NOT-redo
list. Product labels was the obvious pick on volume and is NOT here — it was
made twice in July 2026, and the 2024 version still outranks both remakes.

Only four rows, deliberately. Nothing built in the new code-rendered format has
been public long enough to rank, so there is **no evidence yet on whether the
new format wins**. The 21–27 Sep publications answer that. Ranking ten rows now
would be guessing; re-rank rows 5+ in mid-October with real data.

Check the catalogue for CLUSTER SIZE before ranking — a big cluster total can be six
of our own videos splitting it, which makes a seventh pointless. Watch-time-per-view
is the better tiebreaker than raw views. Ties break on **funnel strength, not views** — the channel exists to sell the
£4.99 packs and the £9.99/mo Club, and to survive YouTube deciding something.
Ad revenue is the smallest lever: at the new-cohort RPM of £3.23, one £4.99 sale
equals about 1,545 views of ad money.

